{title: Blest Be the Tie That Binds}
{artist: John Fawcett / Hans G. Nägeli}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 3/4}
{score: blest-be-the-tie-that-binds.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Blest be the tie that [C]binds
Our [G]hearts in Chris[D]tian [G]love
The [G]fellowship of [C]kindred [G]minds
Is [Em]like to [D]that a[G]bove
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Before our Father's [C]throne
We [G]pour our ar[D]dent [G]prayers
Our [G]fears, our hopes, our [C]aims are [G]one
Our [Em]comforts [D]and our [G]cares
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]We share our mutual [C]woes
Our [G]mutual bur[D]dens [G]bear
And [G]often for each [C]other [G]flows
The [Em]sympa[D]thizing [G]tear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]When we asunder [C]part
It [G]gives us in[D]ward [G]pain
But [G]we shall still be [C]joined in [G]heart
And [Em]hope to [D]meet a[G]gain
{end_of_verse}
